# Patterns here are matched against the full path from the context root, so a bare `node_modules/`
# would only ever match one at the top level — and every one of these actually lives a directory down,
# in frontend/ or backend/InstaGraph.Api/. Hence the `**/` on each. Getting this wrong is not a tidiness
# problem: `COPY frontend/ ./` would then carry a Windows-built node_modules into a Linux image, and
# npm's native binaries fail there in ways that read as a source error rather than a platform mismatch.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.angular/
**/bin/
**/obj/

**/.git/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/

# Local secrets and local uploads stay local. The image builds its config from appsettings.example.json
# and takes the real secrets from environment variables at run time.
**/appsettings.Development.json
backend/InstaGraph.Api/appsettings.json
backend/InstaGraph.Api/wwwroot/uploads/

*.md
InstaGraph.sql
